window.docContents[20].resolve({"/part-4-frameworks/ch13-superstructures/#ch13-superstructures":{"contents":"Given a base set X of individuals (urelements), the cumulative superstructure V(X) builds every finite-rank set-theoretic object over X:\n\nV_0(X) = X, \\qquad V_{n+1}(X) = V_n(X) \\cup \\mathcal{P}\\bigl(V_n(X)\\bigr), \\qquad V(X) = \\bigcup_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}} V_n(X).\n\nUsing Kuratowski ordered pairs (a, b) = \\{\\{a\\}, \\{a, b\\}\\}, relations and functions on V_n(X) reside cleanly inside V_{n+3}(X). A Nonstandard Framework for X consists of a map a \\mapsto {}^*a from V(X) into V({}^*X) satisfying Łoś / Zakon Bounded-Quantifier (\\Delta_0) Transfer: every formula whose quantifiers are bounded to entities \\forall x \\in A or \\exists x \\in A holds in V(X) iff its *-transform holds in V({}^*X)!\n\n\n\nIn Ch13_UniversesFrameworks.lean (our largest module at 12,047 lines), we formalize the full quotient construction of Entity X from RawStage X m, Kuratowski pairs and n-tuples, internal set comprehension, the Zakon collapsed ultrapower framework, and the exact bridge proving that our Chapter 11–12 internal sets and partial functions coincide with internal entities in V(\\mathbb{R}^*)!\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch13\n\n-- Superstructure entities and agreement between Ch12 internal functions and V(ℝ*):\n#check Entity\n#check @isInternalFun_iff_isInternalEntity_partialFunToEntity\n#check @isInternalFun_total_iff_mem_star_funSpace\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part IV — Nonstandard Frameworks, Enlargements & Saturation","header":"4.1. Chapter 13: Zakon Superstructures &  <missing>  Transfer","id":"/part-4-frameworks/ch13-superstructures/#ch13-superstructures"}});